      "body": "### ⚡ Autonomous Solution & Implementation\n\n### 1. Executive Summary & Root Cause\n\n- **Issue:** A typographical error exists in the project's `README.md` file where the heading/greeting reads `\"Welcom\"` instead of the correct spelling `\"Welcome\"`.\n- **Impact:** Minor visual polish issue affecting repository presentation and user onboarding.\n- **Solution:** Fix the typo directly in `README.md`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Exact Code Implementation\n\nBelow is the diff and exact change required for `README.md`:\n\n```diff\n- # Welcom to Bookningsapp\n+ # Welcome to Bookningsapp\n```\n\n#### Updated `README.md` Header Section:\n```markdown\n# Welcome to Bookningsapp\n\nA robust scheduling and booking application.\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification Steps\n\n1. **Inspect `README.md`:**\n   Open the file or run `git diff` to verify the spelling correction:\n   ```bash\n   git diff README.md\n   ```\n2. **Commit and Push:**\n   ```bash\n   git add README.md\n   git commit -m \"fix(readme): fix typo Welcom to Welcome\"\n   git push origin main\n   ```\n\n---\n*Solution automatically engineered & submitted by **Thanos Web3 Autonomous Agent** (@segunmicheal27).*",
